WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.036
 Doug, Ashley, congratulations.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.105
Your karambits have led you
guys into the final round

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.306
of this competition.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.406
Good job.

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:08.808
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:09.942
to make one of these.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:13.346
[music playing]

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:23.589
The cane sword.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:24.957
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.159
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.031 line:7%
ASHLEY: It's day one.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.300
I'm back in my shop
in Columbus, Ohio,

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:37.370
and I'm going to start working
on a rough blade shape.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.105
This is going to be a very
thin, very light blade.

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:41.941
I don't want to have
excess material that's

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.509
going to come back to bite me.

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:44.977
I'm going to start
with exactly what

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.013
I need and work from there.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:48.581
I can't draw it out too thin.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.751
I'll end up with weird little
weak spots in the middle,

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:54.621
and that's catastrophic
for a blade.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.188
Just cleaning off a little bit.

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:59.959 line:7%
Some pretty gnarly scale on it.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:01.527
I'm checking and I'm grinding.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.297
I don't want to take away
any more than I need to.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.232 line:0%
A little bit more work
in the forge tomorrow,

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.700 line:0%
a little bit more
work on the grinder,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.503 line:0%
and then I'll be
good for a quench.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.306 line:0%
 I'm going to do a
little fireball action

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:15.575 line:7%
here to kick this project off.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.743
I'm a trained professional.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.911
Do you not do this
at home, ever.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.479
3, 2, 1.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:22.381
[explosion]

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.849
[laughs]

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.051
Fireball.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:26.452
Let's get this party started.

00:01:26.518 --> 00:01:29.455
It feels good to be
home in my home shop.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.258
I'm going to take this piece of
5160, and get it in the fire,

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.126
and get it heated,
and get it drawn out.

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:36.062
A little nervous about
it because I only

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:39.865
have one piece of this 5160,
so it's kind of crucial

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.300
that I don't screw it up.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.169
I'm a Damascus guy,
so I'm going to use

00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:47.573
the Damascus for the
pommel and for the burl.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.042 line:0%
There's no way this piece
is getting out of here

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.612 line:7%
without some Damascus on it.

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.248 line:0%
ASHLEY: Starting off day 2,
I've got to do a little bit more

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:58.218 line:0%
of a touch-up work, and then I
should be ready for a quench.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:02.054
All I'm really working on is
straightening out any wiggles.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:05.091
I've still got a
couple, so I'll just

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:08.094
hit and check back and forth.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.430
Things aren't really
trueing up like I'd like,

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:15.668
so I decide I need to just
go into the quench now.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.270
I don't feel any tings.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.570
Comes out of the quench--

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:19.905
[sighs]

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.207
--and there is
definitely a warp.

00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:24.911
I feel like I could
requench it maybe once.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.113
I've got to go in
for a second quench.

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:28.548
Am I going to scrap this blade?

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:30.817
Am I going to start over,
or is this going to work?

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:36.022
I come out of the quench,
skate a file down it.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.924
There's a couple spots
towards the handle that

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.059
are a little softer,
but I think we're

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.827
good to keep moving along.

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:45.164 line:0%
I feel like I can finally a
little bit start to breathe.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.666 line:0%
DOUG: I would have
liked to have gotten

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.969 line:0%
a little further yesterday, but
my quench was very successful.

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:52.438
Daddy likey.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.640
Woo!

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.941
And so it's mechanism day.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.677
The cane sword is
going to require

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:00.713
a locking mechanism
so the sword will lock

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.548
properly in the cane itself.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:05.417
I'm not really tooled up
to do stuff like this.

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:08.253
This locking mechanism
really is a tricky bastard.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.522
The brass hook slides
into the bolster,

00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:14.526
which latches it and locks the
sword into the cane itself.

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:16.296
And that has to
hinge because there

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:19.132
has to be a spring underneath
it that will allow the button

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.601
to compress down to where
it releases the lock,

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.837
and then the spring will
push the hook back up to lock

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:27.774
into place in the bolster.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.309
Yeah, I got a latch.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:33.846 line:0%
All I have to do is attach my
button to it and tap this in,

00:03:33.912 --> 00:03:35.615 line:7%
and I'm on my way.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.350 line:0%
ASHLEY: I've never
made a cane before,

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:40.052 line:0%
so today I want to spend a
whole day dedicated to it.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.587
I want to make
sure that this cane

00:03:41.653 --> 00:03:43.655
is structurally solid in case
they're going to beat on it.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.692
So my cane is going to
be a framed construction.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:50.897
This bit will be in the
middle of two other slabs,

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:55.468
kind of like this one, and
it'll all be pinned together

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:57.570
as well as a fair bit of epoxy.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.407
Beautiful.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.409
I'm taking my cane
down from being a box

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.212
to being a hexagonal shape.

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:07.913
It's starting to really
look like something

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.682
other than a block of wood.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.751
So I've done the
texturing on my cane.

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:15.387
That's very similar to the flint
knapp that we did in round 2

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:17.290
on the handles of our karambits.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.358 line:0%
All that's left is I want
to pop a little linseed oil

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:24.196 line:0%
on all the wood parts
and, I mean, I'm done.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:25.431 line:7%
DOUG: Last day.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:29.368
First thing I have
to do is make a cane.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:32.204
It's a little wobbly
and rough, but I

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:33.739
think it gives it character.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:37.109
We're going to sand it down
really smooth and then oil it.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.377
It'll be great.

00:04:38.443 --> 00:04:40.779
This is my Damascus
billet for the pommel.

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:44.250
That's carbon steel, so carbon
steel doesn't like this.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:47.319 line:0%
The Damascus pommel has
to be tapped so that it

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.588 line:0%
will screw on the
bolt that I've welded

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.124 line:7%
into the tang of the sword.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:54.093 line:0%
If I break the tap off
in here, that's it.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.562 line:0%
Oh, god, I wish I
had another tap.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.266
There it is.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:02.968
Sure enough, it breaks.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.071
[bleep] damn it.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.339
Failure is not an
option, so I'm going

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:09.542
to go to my plan B,
which is building

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.510
one out of a piece of rosewood.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:15.447
It bums me out because the
rosewood pommel isn't as pretty

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:18.617
as the Damascus one, but
I'm just going to have

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.320
to settle with the rosewood.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.121
It's going to be a good weapon.

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:24.323
There we go.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.191
Button's working.

00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:27.726
It'll definitely hurt somebody.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:30.863
And if you've got a bad
leg, it'll hold you up.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:31.863
[laughs]

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.834
[music playing]

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:43.208
 Doug, Ashley, welcome
back, and welcome

00:05:43.308 --> 00:05:45.578
to the frozen great outdoors.

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:47.980
You guys have had four
days at your home forges

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.281
to work on your cane swords.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.117
Doug, how did it go?

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.652 line:0%
 It proved to be a
difficult build for me.

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:55.554 line:7%
I built the blade out of 5160.

00:05:55.654 --> 00:06:00.392 line:0%
It's a black-walnut cane and
handle with a rosewood pommel.

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:03.762 line:7%
The bolsters are Damascus.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.397
It was tough.

00:06:05.497 --> 00:06:07.433
 All right, Ashley,
how'd it go for you?

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:10.669 line:0%
 I kept mine pretty
straightforward.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:14.573 line:0%
I did a 5160 blade, brass
pins here and there,

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.244 line:0%
and a copper connector to
a black-and-white ebony

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.480 line:7%
little stop at the bottom.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.548
 All right, bladesmiths, your
weapons will now be put through

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:24.617
a series of three
tests-- a strength test,

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:26.952
a sharpness test, and
up first, the kill test.

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:27.720
Doug.

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:33.226
DOUG: All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:35.394
The cane sword, what
an elegant way to walk

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:37.996
around with a concealed weapon.

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:39.998
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:06:40.098 --> 00:06:42.234
I will take your cane sword
and deliver killing slashes and

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.070
blows to this ballistics dummy.

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:45.437
Doug, you're up first.
You ready?

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:46.405
 I'm ready.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:47.039
 All right, let's do this.

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:48.340
 All right.

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:50.475
I'm really nervous
about today's testing.

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.044
Anything could go wrong.

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:55.414
I'm hoping to do as much damage
to the mannequin as possible.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.316
But, you know, I
just-- no matter what,

00:06:57.416 --> 00:06:58.917
I don't want anything to break.

00:06:59.017 --> 00:07:02.522
[rock music]

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.442
 Are you kidding me?

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:27.046
 [laughs] All right.

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:30.248
 All right, Doug, let's
talk about your cane sword.

00:07:30.315 --> 00:07:33.052
You have a very sharp edge.

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:35.387
This blade thrusts nicely.

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:36.589
It cuts nicely.

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:39.091
And who knew such
a very slim blade

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.593
could do that much damage?

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:42.094
What I love about
your handle right

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:44.797
here is that curved part right
there gives me that flair

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:48.400
that I like to feel when
I'm thrusting or slashing

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.302
and moving a weapon around.

00:07:50.368 --> 00:07:53.138
Your weapon, sir, it will kill.

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:54.406
 Thank you very much.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:55.541
 All right, Ashley,
it's your turn.

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:56.374
Are you ready, sir?

00:07:56.441 --> 00:07:57.143
 Absolutely.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:57.844
 Let's do this.

00:08:01.246 --> 00:08:03.483
 Tough act to follow.

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:07.320
This is the kill test, and
a cane sword has to kill.

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:09.555
If it doesn't, this is
the end of the line.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.165
[rock music]

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.167
Oh!

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:27.039
There it was.

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.774
 Bro, I'm sorry.

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:29.842
 It's all right.

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:37.849
 All right, Ashley, let's talk
about your cane sword here.

00:08:37.916 --> 00:08:40.419
The cross actually shows here
that it is kind of coarse,

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:42.655
so it could be a
heat-tempering issue.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:46.759
But worse than that, some of
the grinds here are uneven,

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:49.495
and this was its thinnest spot.

00:08:49.561 --> 00:08:51.864
So as you can see, it's
a critical failure.

00:08:54.266 --> 00:08:56.468
 Well, Ashley, when we have
a tough break on this show,

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:57.836
it's literal.

00:08:57.903 --> 00:09:00.372
You suffered a catastrophic
failure and cannot

00:09:00.438 --> 00:09:01.707
continue in this competition.

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.175
And for that reason,
I'd like to invite

00:09:03.275 --> 00:09:04.910
you to please leave the range.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:08.514
DOUG: It's heartbreaking, but I
am incredibly proud of the work

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:09.882
that I've done.

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:12.084
When I get home, the first
thing I'm going to do

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:14.320
is make another cane sword.

00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:17.156
I-- I got to do it
right at least once.

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:17.956
That's how it goes.

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:18.791
 Tough break.

00:09:24.329 --> 00:09:25.597
 Doug, congratulations.

00:09:25.697 --> 00:09:27.633
You are the new "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.169
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:32.103
How do you feel right now?

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:33.839
 $10,000 richer.

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:35.240
[laughter]

00:09:35.307 --> 00:09:37.375
 All right, come on over here
and shake our hands, brother.

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:38.410
DOUG: I did it.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:39.144
I did it.

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.413
 Good job, Doug.

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:41.780
DOUG: It's awesome.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.250
This has been one of the
best experiences of my life.

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:46.652
It took me every
emotion possible--

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:50.589
anger, joy, to just
absolute crying.

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:52.724
For anybody out there
that wants to do this,

00:09:52.791 --> 00:09:55.460
my suggestion to you is
show up with your A game

00:09:55.527 --> 00:09:57.830
and get a lot of
sleep before you

00:09:57.896 --> 00:10:02.134
come because you're not going
to get any until it's over.

